From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH wsi 019] panvk/android: zero-copy present into the window buffer

The Android swapchain rendered into a driver-allocated AHardwareBuffer and then
memcpy'd the whole frame into the window's next buffer under
ANativeWindow_lock(). That is a full-frame CPU copy plus a cache-cold AHB read
on every present, and the frame only reaches the compositor once the CPU gets
around to it.

Render straight into the surface instead:

- Resolve the producer-side BufferQueue entry points libnativewindow exports
  for the LLNDK (ANativeWindow_dequeueBuffer/queueBuffer/cancelBuffer,
  ANativeWindowBuffer_getHardwareBuffer, ANativeWindow_setBufferCount,
  ANativeWindow_query) with dlsym; the NDK does not declare them.
- At swapchain creation, follow the vndk/window.h recipe: query the minimum
  number of un-dequeued buffers M, raise the window pool to imageCount + M,
  dequeue imageCount buffers, and import each one's AHardwareBuffer as a
  VkImage through the existing deferred AHB path (so gralloc's real modifier
  and plane layout are used). Then cancel them all back to the window.
- acquire dequeues a buffer, waits its fence and maps it to the image slot;
  a buffer that was never imported means the window reallocated its pool, so it
  is cancelled and the next one is taken. present is a single queueBuffer()
  with no fence: wsi_common_queue_present() already waited for the rendering
  submit.
- release_images cancels a held buffer, destroy cancels whatever is still out.

The copy path stays as the fallback: missing symbols, a geometry or format the
window buffer cannot back, a failed dma-buf import (MTK AFBC buffers are
rejected by some kbase builds) or PANVK_WSI_ZERO_COPY=0 all fall back to it and
log one line.

Purpose: remove the per-frame full-frame CPU copy from the Android present path.
Tested GPU: build only (aarch64-linux-android29-clang), not yet run on device.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: wsi/016, wsi/017, wsi/018.
Validation test: TBD, on-device A/B present smoke test (PANVK_WSI_ZERO_COPY=1/0).

Generated-by: LLM

